the target language is: prolog.

% Spike: sale.l4's contract read over a finished history of timed events --
% the timeless reading of the design notes l4.md, section 4. Expected
% answers are the L4 evaluator's #TRACE results (node l4run.mjs sale.l4).

% The same L4 contract, read over a finished history of timed events
% (an event-calculus reading): which obligation is reached, when, and how it ends.

the templates are:
    *a party* delivers at *a time*; undefined.
    *a party* pays *an amount* at *a time*; undefined.
    the history ends at *a time*; undefined.
    the delivery obligation starts at *a time* with deadline *a deadline*.
    the delivery obligation is fulfilled at *a time*.
    the payment obligation starts at *a time* with deadline *a deadline*.
    the payment obligation is fulfilled at *a time*.
    the sale is fulfilled.
    the sale is breached by *a party* because *a reason*.
    *an obligation* is pending with *a number* days left.

the knowledge base sale includes:

the delivery obligation starts at 0 with deadline 14.

the delivery obligation is fulfilled at a time if
    the delivery obligation starts at a start with deadline a deadline
    and seller delivers at the time
    and the time >= the start
    and the time =< the deadline
    and it is not the case that
        seller delivers at an earlier time
        and the earlier time >= the start
        and the earlier time < the time.

the payment obligation starts at a time with deadline a deadline if
    the delivery obligation is fulfilled at the time
    and the deadline = the time + 30.

the payment obligation is fulfilled at a time if
    the payment obligation starts at a start with deadline a deadline
    and buyer pays 100 at the time
    and the time >= the start
    and the time =< the deadline
    and it is not the case that
        buyer pays 100 at an earlier time
        and the earlier time >= the start
        and the earlier time < the time.

the sale is fulfilled if
    the payment obligation is fulfilled at a time.

the sale is breached by seller because "failed to deliver" if
    the delivery obligation starts at a start with deadline a deadline
    and the history ends at an end
    and the end > the deadline
    and it is not the case that
        the delivery obligation is fulfilled at a time.

the sale is breached by buyer because "failed to pay" if
    the payment obligation starts at a start with deadline a deadline
    and the history ends at an end
    and the end > the deadline
    and it is not the case that
        the payment obligation is fulfilled at a time.

delivery is pending with a number days left if
    the delivery obligation starts at a start with deadline a deadline
    and the history ends at an end
    and the end =< the deadline
    and it is not the case that
        the delivery obligation is fulfilled at a time
    and the number = the deadline - the end.

payment is pending with a number days left if
    the payment obligation starts at a start with deadline a deadline
    and the history ends at an end
    and the end =< the deadline
    and it is not the case that
        the payment obligation is fulfilled at a time
    and the number = the deadline - the end.

query fulfilled is:
    the sale is fulfilled.

query breached is:
    the sale is breached by which party because which reason.

query pending is:
    which obligation is pending with which number days left.

scenario on_time is:
    seller delivers at 10.
    buyer pays 100 at 20.
    the history ends at 20.
    fulfilled expects answers ["the sale is fulfilled"].
    breached expects answers [].

scenario late is:
    seller delivers at 10.
    buyer pays 100 at 50.
    the history ends at 50.
    fulfilled expects answers [].
    breached expects answers ["the sale is breached by buyer because failed to pay"].

scenario unfinished is:
    seller delivers at 10.
    the history ends at 10.
    pending expects answers ["payment is pending with 30 days left"].

scenario early_payment is:
    buyer pays 100 at 5.
    the history ends at 5.
    pending expects answers ["delivery is pending with 9 days left"].

scenario wrong_amount is:
    seller delivers at 10.
    buyer pays 99 at 20.
    the history ends at 20.
    pending expects answers ["payment is pending with 20 days left"].

scenario early_payment_then_wait is:
    buyer pays 100 at 5.
    the history ends at 20.
    breached expects answers ["the sale is breached by seller because failed to deliver"].

scenario delivered_on_the_last_day is:
    seller delivers at 14.
    the history ends at 14.
    pending expects answers ["payment is pending with 30 days left"].

scenario paid_on_the_last_day is:
    seller delivers at 10.
    buyer pays 100 at 40.
    the history ends at 40.
    fulfilled expects answers ["the sale is fulfilled"].
